## Filament Rich Editor Toolkit (asignua/filament-rich-editor-toolkit)

- Ten independent pieces for the Filament 5 `RichEditor`: `PasteCleanPlugin`, `CustomAttributesPlugin`, `EmbedPlugin`, `ImageUrlPlugin`, `ImagePropertiesPlugin`, `LinkOptionsPlugin`, `FullscreenPlugin`, `CharacterCountPlugin`, `SourceCodePlugin` (all `Asignua\RichEditorToolkit\Plugins\*`, added with `RichEditor::make()->plugins([X::make()])`) and the panel plugin `Asignua\RichEditorToolkit\StickyToolbarPlugin`.
- A toolbar button exists only when it is listed in `->toolbarButtons([...])`: `cleanFormat`, `embed`, `imageUrl`, `imageProperties`, `linkOptions`, `fullscreen`, `sourceCode`. An unknown button name makes Filament throw.
- Run `php artisan filament:assets` after install/upgrade: the editor imports `resources/dist/*.js` by URL. A missing publish is a 404 and a silent `console.error`, the module is simply absent.
- Plugins with a server half (`CustomAttributesPlugin`, `EmbedPlugin`, `ImagePropertiesPlugin`, `LinkOptionsPlugin`) MUST also be in the front-end renderer, otherwise the data sits in the database and vanishes on the page: render with `RichEditorToolkit::renderer($content)->toHtml()` (`links: false` / `images: false`, or config `rich-editor-toolkit.renderer.link_options|image_properties`, switch `LinkOptionsPlugin` / `ImagePropertiesPlugin` off at render time; both default ON), or add `RichEditorToolkit::plugins()` to your own `RichContentRenderer` and render it with `RichEditorToolkit::toHtml($renderer)` (its own `toHtml()` uses Filament's shared sanitizer, which the toolkit never extends). Per-field `CustomAttributesPlugin::make()->attributes([...])`/`->types([...])` must be repeated in `RichEditorToolkit::renderer($content, attributes: [...], types: [...])`. `PasteCleanPlugin` has NO server half and must NOT be added to the renderer (a second pass would strip the attributes the other plugin keeps).
- Attribute allow-list = `class`, `id`, `style` + `rich-editor-toolkit.attributes` config (explicit names; Symfony's sanitizer has no `data-*` wildcard). `on*`, URL attributes (`href`, `src`, `srcset`, `srcdoc`, `action`, `formaction`, ...), `is`, names with `:` and framework directives (`x-*`, `hx-*`, `v-*`, `ng-*`, `wire:*`) are never accepted; list only what you need (`data-*`, `aria-*`, `role`). Node types missing from the built-in list: `rich-editor-toolkit.types`. A name the node declares itself wins: `id` on an `<img>` is NOT kept (Filament's image owns `id` as the media key, `data-id`), `class`/`style` are. The PHP list (`Extensions\CustomAttributes::TYPES`) and `resources/js/src/custom-attributes.js` `DEFAULT_TYPES` must stay identical (a test pins it).
- Embeds: YouTube/Vimeo links are parsed by `Support\VideoEmbed` and rebuilt (youtube-nocookie, no autoplay); other hosts need `rich-editor-toolkit.embed.hosts` (`host` or `host/path/prefix`, https only, prefix matched on a segment boundary, dot segments refused). The `src` is checked when HTML is parsed AND when a node is rendered (JSON content). `sandbox`/`allow`/`referrerpolicy`/`loading` are forced on render.
- `ImagePropertiesPlugin` (`imageProperties` button, enabled only while an image is selected; also usable in the floating toolbar: `->floatingToolbars(fn ($c) => [...$c->getDefaultFloatingToolbars(), 'image' => ['imageProperties']])`): alt text, "decorative" (`alt=""`, kept as empty, distinct from a missing alt), a plain-text caption, `left|center|right`. Core Filament already edits alt in "Attach files"; this does not duplicate it. It SHADOWS the `image` node (lower priority in JS like `listItem`, higher priority subclass of `ImageExtension` in PHP). Markup is `<span class="asignua-rte-figure asignua-rte-align-X"><img><span class="asignua-rte-caption">` and NOT `<figure>`: Filament's image is inline inside `<p>`, a `<figure>` there is invalid; a typed/pasted `<figure>` is read and rewritten (`adopt()` turns the wrapper into the image in place, in JS and PHP alike, so no wrapper child leaks into the document JSON). A plain image stays a bare stock `<img>`. Alignment is a whitelist, caption is escaped. Optional front CSS: `vendor:publish --tag=filament-rich-editor-toolkit-front-css`. PHP/JS constants (`asignua-rte-*`, `data-asignua-*`) are pinned by a test.
- `LinkOptionsPlugin` (`linkOptions` button, enabled only inside a link): "open in a new tab" + rel `nofollow|sponsored|ugc`, written with `updateAttributes('link', …)` on the link under the cursor. A SECOND button on purpose (Filament's `LinkAction` has no seam; rich-links writes into the same mark) and it has NO browser module. The renderer half (`Support\LinkAttributes::apply()` over the sanitized HTML, enabled when the plugin is in the renderer): `target` is `_blank` or dropped, `rel` is filtered to `link_options.rel_tokens`, `_blank` forces `noopener noreferrer`; `link_options.external_rel` / `->externalRel([...])` adds tokens to absolute links leaving the site at RENDER time only (`app.url` host + `internal_hosts` are the site). Re-setting the address with the stock link button drops the `rel`. Do not shadow the `link` mark in tiptap-php: marks are not de-duplicated by name there (the opening tag would be written twice), unlike nodes.
- `PasteCleanPlugin::make()->uploadImages()` (`paste_clean.upload_images`, off by default): Word / Google Docs pictures are uploaded instead of removed. `resources/js/src/paste-images.js` (priority 1000 so its `handlePaste` runs before Filament's `localFiles`) snapshots the clipboard, turns `file:///` images into `data:` URLs from `text/rtf` (`extractRtfPictures`, matched BY ORDER, a count mismatch matches nothing) and Google Docs images via the modal-less editor action `asignuaFetchRemoteImage` (a modal-less action's return value reaches the browser: `await $wire.mountAction(name, args, {schemaComponent: key})`), then re-dispatches a plain `paste` Event with a stand-in `clipboardData`; Filament's own pasted-`data:`-image upload does the rest. Only on fields with file attachments (`attachFiles` button or `->fileAttachments()`; the `localFiles` extension is the source of `$wire`, key, accepted types, max size). The server download is an SSRF primitive: keep every gate of `Support\RemoteImageFetcher` (https/443, host allow-list, ALL resolved addresses public, connection pinned, no redirects, byte cap, magic-byte type) and never return exception messages to the browser. The request goes out WITHOUT a proxy, is never decompressed and writes into a capped sink; the action needs a logged-in user by default (`paste_clean.remote_image_guests`, `->authorizeRemoteImages(bool|Closure)`), is rate limited per viewer and per viewer+field, and a wildcard host over a public suffix (`*.co.uk`) matches nothing (the list lives in PHP `RemoteImageFetcher::PUBLIC_SUFFIXES` and JS `PUBLIC_SUFFIXES`, pinned by `tests/fixtures/host-allow.json`). Do not use `CURLOPT_MAXFILESIZE_LARGE` in the Guzzle `curl` option: Guzzle 8 rejects it.
- `FullscreenPlugin` (`fullscreen` button): fixed overlay at z-index 35, deliberately NOT the browser top layer (it would hide Filament's modals opened from the toolbar); Esc leaves. It and `CharacterCountPlugin` need no panel plugin: their JS modules link `filament-rich-editor-toolkit-ui.css` themselves (URL passed in the module's query string).
- `SourceCodePlugin` (`sourceCode` button): swaps the editing area for a textarea with the pretty-printed HTML (`source-html.js`; `<pre>` untouched). The edit returns ONLY through the schema (`editor.commands.setContent(html, { emitUpdate: true })`), so unknown markup is dropped and a status notice says so (`materiallyDiffers()`: ignores whitespace, attribute order, `<b>`/`<strong>`, attributes the editor added; strict otherwise). It syncs 400 ms after typing, on blur/change, on any Ctrl/Cmd keydown (Filament's mod+s), on Livewire's `commit` hook (best effort), on the form's `submit` (capture) and on leaving, so Save while in source mode keeps the source. A document change that is not its own sync (the server rewrites attachment ids; TipTap's `setContent` from Filament emits only a transaction, not `update`) rebuilds the textarea from the editor (`refresh()` from `onTransaction`), so a stale textarea can never overwrite it. Other toolbar tools are disabled meanwhile (matched by handler name `asignuaToggleSourceCode|Fullscreen`). `class`/`id`/`style`/`data-*` survive only with `CustomAttributesPlugin`. Tab is not trapped. No server half: not in the renderer. Config `source_code.indent`.
- Length limits: `RichEditor::make('body')->textLength(max: 500, maxWords: 80, min: 20)` adds `Rules\RichTextLength` AND the counter (`plugins()` appends in Filament, so it composes). Both count PLAIN TEXT with one definition (`Support\PlainText` in PHP, `resources/js/src/character-count.js`; the shared fixture `tests/fixtures/text-length.json` is run against both): blocks joined by newline, characters = code points without newlines, words = runs of non-whitespace, atoms add nothing. Changing the definition means changing both sides and the fixtures. The counter only displays; the rule is the enforcement. Empty text passes `min` (use `required`).
- `PasteCleanPlugin::make()->strict()` (or `paste_clean.strict`): a paste is cut down to the field's toolbar. The JS reads the rendered toolbar buttons' Alpine class binding (`isActive('bold', [])`, heading level in the options JSON) in `resources/js/src/paste-strict.js`; an unreadable toolbar restricts nothing. A test pins the markup shape. Off by default; also applies to in-editor pastes.
- Rebuild the JS after editing `resources/js/src/*`: `npm run build` (commit `resources/dist`), test with `npm run test:js`.
